=== SCHEMA ===
migrations/000170_snapshots_si.up.sql defines, in order:

  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS climate_snapshots        CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS motor_snapshots          CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS security_events          CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tire_pressure_snapshots  CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS media_snapshots          CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS safety_snapshots         CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS location_snapshots       CASCADE;

  CREATE TABLE climate_snapshots ( ... PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts) );
    34 columns total. SI temperatures: inside_temp_c, outside_temp_c,
    hvac_left_request_c, hvac_right_request_c,
    cabin_overheat_protection_temperature_limit_c. Booleans for HVAC
    AC/Auto/Power/Defrost/Preconditioning/SeatBelt/Vent flags.
    Integers for fan speed, seat heater levels, seat cooling levels,
    steering-wheel heat level. TEXT for fan status / defrost mode /
    climate keeper mode / cabin overheat protection mode /
    rear seat heaters mode.

  CREATE TABLE motor_snapshots ( ... PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts) );
    37 columns total. Per-corner (front / rear / rear_left / rear_right):
      *_torque_nm         (DiTorqueActual* in Newton-meters, SI)
      *_stator_c          (DiStatorTemp* in Celsius, SI)
      *_inverter_c        (DiInverterT* in Celsius, SI)
      *_heatsink_c        (DiHeatsinkT* in Celsius, SI)
      *_axle_speed_rpm    (DiAxleSpeed* in RPM; UnitKindNone in protomodel)
      *_motor_current_a   (DiMotorCurrent* in Amperes, SI)
      *_vbat_v            (DiVBat* in Volts, SI)
      *_state             (DiState* enum; TEXT)
    Plus power_w (Watts), torque_motor_nm, torque_command_nm
    (DiSlaveTorqueCmd / DiTorquemotor; UnitKindNone but Nm), hvil_state
    (Hvil enum), isolation_resistance_ohm.
    The per-corner layout supports tri-motor (Plaid: F + REL + RER) and
    quad-motor (Cybertruck: F + R + REL + RER) configurations without
    schema changes; single-motor / dual-motor cars simply leave the
    extra columns NULL.

  CREATE TABLE security_events (
    vehicle_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
    ts         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    event_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    from_state TEXT,
    to_state   TEXT,
    details    JSONB,
    PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts, event_type));
    Append-only event log; downstream consumers INSERT only, no
    UPDATE. PK includes event_type so two distinct event kinds at the
    same `ts` remain insertable. Two indexes: (vehicle_id, ts DESC)
    and (event_type, ts DESC).

  CREATE TABLE tire_pressure_snapshots ( ... PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts) );
    15 columns. Per-corner pressure (front_left/front_right/rear_left/
    rear_right) in Pascals (_pa); per-corner status TEXT; per-corner
    last_seen_at TIMESTAMPTZ (TpmsLastSeenPressureTime*); fleet-level
    hard_warnings + soft_warnings TEXT (TpmsHardWarnings/TpmsSoftWarnings).

  CREATE TABLE media_snapshots ( ... PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts) );
    13 columns. track_name/artist/album/station/source/play_status TEXT;
    volume_pct/volume_max/volume_increment INTEGER; duration_s/elapsed_s
    INTEGER (seconds, SI). Source fields: MediaPlaybackStatus,
    MediaPlaybackSource, MediaAudioVolume, MediaAudioVolumeMax,
    MediaAudioVolumeIncrement, MediaNowPlaying{Title,Artist,Album,
    Station,Duration,Elapsed}.

  CREATE TABLE safety_snapshots ( ... PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts) );
    6 columns: service_mode + service_mode_plus BOOLEAN, wiper_state +
    crash_state TEXT (continuous-value flags; the corresponding
    state-change events ALSO append to security_events).

  CREATE TABLE location_snapshots ( ... PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts) );
    6 columns: place / country / region TEXT (geocoded labels);
    geocoded_at TIMESTAMPTZ (lookup wall-clock; lets a stale row be
    detected without re-geocoding). Raw lat/lng/altitude/heading live
    in `positions` (prompt 0030).

WHY DROP TABLE IF EXISTS at the top of every block:
  The pre-phase-42 snapshot tables created in 000142_baseline_typed
  (climate_snapshots, motor_snapshots, security_events,
  tire_pressure_snapshots, ...) were dropped wholesale by
  000146_drop_snapshot_tables; none of them currently exist. The
  redundant DROP at the top makes this migration self-healing if a
  developer reapplies an old database snapshot, and it mirrors the
  defensive pattern phase-42 prompt 0030 used for `positions`.
  CASCADE is safe — a grep over migrations/ found zero
  `REFERENCES <snapshot>(...)` clauses, so no other table depends on
  any of these.

WHY column-name suffix carries the unit (ADR-004 #4):
  Every unit-bearing numeric column lives in canonical SI and the unit
  suffix is part of the column name. This makes the SI contract self-
  documenting and audit-grep-able. The forbidden-suffix scan in the
  gate enforces the "no wire-format units in column names" rule.

WHY rpm and ohm columns are not converted:
  - axle_speed_rpm: rotational speed. Not a linear-velocity field,
    therefore not converted by units.ToSI (UnitKindNone in protomodel,
    matching internal/tesla/units/conversions.go's documented exclusion
    of DiAxleSpeed* from speedFields). RPM is the field's natural unit.
  - isolation_resistance_ohm: Ohms are SI base for resistance
    (V/A = Ω). No conversion needed.

WHY temperatures are stored in Celsius rather than Kelvin:
  internal/tesla/units/conversions.go documents Celsius as the
  canonical SI form for temperature in this codebase (the alternative
  Kelvin would be 273.15K higher than every Celsius value, and Tesla
  already produces values in Celsius after the °F→°C conversion).

WHY no compression / retention policies in this migration:
  Phase-42 prompt 0030 (positions) deliberately omitted compression
  and retention policies, deferring those operational decisions to a
  later prompt. This migration follows the same convention so the
  policy-tuning prompt can apply them uniformly across all hot tables.

